  sg_found_intro: { en: `The Quran commands prayer many times and names its essential parts: purification, fixed times, facing the qiblah, standing, recitation, bowing, prostration and humility. But it does not list the number of units, the words said in each position, or their exact order. Allah gave that explanation to His Messenger ﷺ, who taught it by praying in front of the Companions and correcting those who prayed wrongly. So the method of prayer is known from the Quran together with the Sunnah, and the two cannot be separated.`, ms: ``, tur: ``, urd: ``, ben: ``, fas: ``, zh: ``, yue: ``, ja: ``, ru: ``, es: ``, ko: ``, ta: ``, si: `` },
